   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "The imperfect (*era*, *existía*, *carecía*, *se parecía*) is the natural tense for painting a standing scene -- what a city was like, what it lacked, what it resembled -- before a preterite verb (*se convirtió*, *abrió*, *cambió*) marks the moment everything shifted. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know the imperfect (*era*, *tenía*) from A2 Unit 21: it describes how things were and what used to happen. In history it paints the scene before you tell an event: *Buenos Aires crecía*, *las ciudades tenían tranvías*."
+    },
+    {
+      "type": "table",
+      "title": "Imperfect endings",
+      "rows": [
