@@ -1,35 +1,37 @@
 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.cambiosocial.02.subjuntivo-duda",
-  "title": "Subjuntivo de duda: no está claro que...",
+  "title": "Reporting what others say: según and decir que",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "Expressions of doubt or improbability -- *no es evidente que*, *dudo que*, *no parece probable que*, *es poco probable que* -- all trigger the subjunctive, the natural mood for a historian hedging a claim about how solid a social category really was. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know how to report information with *según* from B1 Unit 13. With *según* + the source you say who tells us something, and with *decir que* you report what people said. Historians do this all the time."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "No es evidente que esta nueva clase media compartiera una identidad tan clara como la de la vieja oligarquía terrateniente.",
-          "english": "It's not obvious that this new middle class shared as clear an identity as that of the old landed oligarchy."
+          "spanish": "Según muchos historiadores, aparecieron nuevas clases sociales.",
+          "english": "According to many historians, new social classes appeared."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Dudo que un abogado, un maestro de escuela y un empleado de banco se hubieran visto a sí mismos, en 1890, como parte de un mismo grupo social.",
-          "english": "I doubt that a lawyer, a schoolteacher and a bank clerk would have seen themselves, in 1890, as part of the same social group."
+          "spanish": "Según los historiadores, la clase media pedía más participación política.",
+          "english": "According to historians, the middle class was asking for more political participation."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "No parece probable que la vieja élite terrateniente imaginara, a mediados de siglo, esta clase de competencia.",
-          "english": "It doesn't seem likely that the old landed elite imagined, by mid-century, this kind of competition."
+          "spanish": "Muchos obreros decían que necesitaban sindicatos para defender sus salarios.",
+          "english": "Many workers said that they needed unions to defend their wages."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Es poco probable que estas nuevas clases sociales se hubieran formado con la misma rapidez sin el auge exportador.",
-          "english": "It's unlikely that these new social classes would have formed as quickly without the export boom."
+          "spanish": "Los patrones decían que los sindicatos eran un peligro para el orden.",
+          "english": "The bosses said that the unions were a danger to order."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Compare *es poco probable que* (subjunctive, doubt) with *es cierto que* / *está claro que* (indicative, certainty) -- the same fact can be framed either way, and the mood you choose signals how confident the writer actually is."
+      "content": "After *según* there is no *que*: *Según los historiadores, …*. After *decir que* the verb usually moves back in time when you report the past: the workers said \"we need unions\", so *decían que necesitaban sindicatos*."
     }
   ]
 }
diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-cambiosocial-03-para-que-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-cambiosocial-03-para-que-gr.json
