 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.cambiosocial.03.para-que",
-  "title": "Subjuntivo de finalidad: para que",
+  "title": "Formal phrases: a través de, por medio de, mediante",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "*Para que* (so that, in order that) always takes the subjunctive when the subject of the purpose clause differs from the subject doing the acting -- perfect for describing deliberate policy, where a government or a landlord acted so that someone else would do something. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know *mediante* (\"by means of\") from B1 Unit 24. It is a formal prepositional phrase of means, and a noun follows it directly. Here you use similar phrases to say how people travelled and settled: *a través de* (\"through\") and *por medio de* (\"by means of\")."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Para que Argentina prosperara, argumentaba Alberdi, era necesario atraer masivamente inmigrantes europeos.",
-          "english": "For Argentina to prosper, Alberdi argued, it was necessary to massively attract European immigrants."
+          "spanish": "Muchos conseguían información sobre el trabajo a través de cartas de familiares y amigos.",
+          "english": "Many got information about work through letters from relatives and friends."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Estas políticas fueron diseñadas precisamente para que millones de europeos cruzaran el Atlántico.",
-          "english": "These policies were designed precisely so that millions of Europeans would cross the Atlantic."
+          "spanish": "El gobierno pagaba el pasaje por medio de programas especiales.",
+          "english": "The government paid the passage by means of special programmes."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Fundaron, para que sus comunidades pudieran ayudarse mutuamente, cientos de sociedades de socorros mutuos.",
-          "english": "They founded, so that their communities could help each other, hundreds of mutual aid societies."
-        },
-        {
-          "spanish": "Los gobiernos promovieron la llegada de colonos europeos para que poblaran territorios que consideraban insuficientemente aprovechados.",
-          "english": "Governments promoted the arrival of European settlers so that they would populate territories they considered insufficiently used."
+          "spanish": "Mediante su trabajo y sus negocios, los inmigrantes cambiaron la comida y la música.",
+          "english": "Through their work and their businesses, the immigrants changed the food and the music."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Don't confuse *para que* + subjunctive (different subjects: A acts so that B happens) with *para* + infinitive (same subject: A acts in order to do something themselves) -- *fundaron sociedades para que sus comunidades pudieran*... vs. simply *fundaron sociedades para ayudar a sus comunidades*."
+      "content": "*A través de* and *por medio de* end in *de*, and then a noun follows: *a través de cartas*, *por medio de programas*. Do not drop the *de* (not *a través cartas*). *Mediante* needs no *de*."
     }
   ]
