 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.cambiosocial.04.conjunciones-temporales",
-  "title": "Subjuntivo con conjunciones temporales: cuando, hasta que, antes de que",
+  "title": "The passive with ser: strikes and repression",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "*Antes de que* always takes the subjunctive, no matter the tense. *Hasta que* takes the subjunctive when the event was still pending at the reference point (*esperaban hasta que el gobierno respondiera* -- they were waiting for a response that hadn't come yet). *Cuando*, by contrast, takes the indicative when it introduces a real, completed past event (*cuando el gobierno decidió*...) -- the same conjunction family, but only some of them force uncertainty into the mood. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know the passive with *ser* + past participle from B1 Unit 18. The participle agrees with the subject, and *por* names who did the action. It suits news and history: *La huelga fue reprimida por el ejército*."
+    },
+    {
+      "type": "table",
+      "title": "Passive with ser",
+      "rows": [
+        [
+          "fue reprimida",
+          "was put down (la huelga)"
+        ],
+        [
+          "fueron deportados",
+          "were deported (los dirigentes)"
+        ],
+        [
+          "eran dirigidos",
+          "were led (los sindicatos)"
+        ]
+      ]
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Estas ideas encontraron eco entre los trabajadores, hasta que se convirtieron en organización sindical concreta.",
-          "english": "These ideas found an echo among the workers, until they turned into concrete union organization."
+          "spanish": "La huelga fue reprimida por el ejército.",
+          "english": "The strike was put down by the army."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Esperaban allí, pacíficamente, hasta que el gobierno respondiera a sus peticiones.",
-          "english": "They waited there, peacefully, until the government would respond to their demands."
+          "spanish": "Muchos dirigentes fueron deportados.",
+          "english": "Many leaders were deported."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "El conflicto no hizo más que intensificarse antes de que terminara la década.",
-          "english": "The conflict only intensified before the decade ended."
+          "spanish": "Los sindicatos eran dirigidos por anarquistas y por socialistas.",
+          "english": "The unions were led by anarchists and socialists."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Nunca se estableció una cifra exacta antes de que el hecho quedara, durante décadas, prácticamente silenciado.",
-          "english": "An exact figure was never established before the event remained, for decades, practically silenced."
+          "spanish": "La protesta fue terminada a tiros por el ejército.",
