 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.economiasexportacion.01.comparativos",
-  "title": "Comparativos: el viejo modelo frente al nuevo",
+  "title": "Relative clauses: the products that each country exported",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "Weighing an old economic system against a new one calls for comparatives at every turn: *más/menos... que* for a clear difference, *cuanto más... más* for a rule that scales together. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know relative clauses with *que* and *quien* from B1 Unit 5. A relative clause adds information to a noun and tells us which one we mean. History texts use it all the time: *the products that each country exported*, *the capital that paid for the railways*."
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "El comercio se volvió más libre que antes, pero la región siguió exportando sobre todo materias primas.",
