@@ -1,35 +1,51 @@
 {
-  "id": "grammar.b1.economiasexportacion.05.condicional-hipotetico",
-  "title": "Condicional hipotético: si + pretérito imperfecto de subjuntivo",
+  "id": "grammar.b1.economiasexportacion.05.dejar-de",
+  "title": "Stopping: dejar de + infinitive",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "To ask \"what if\" about a past that didn't happen, pair *si + past subjunctive* (*hubiera invertido*) with the *conditional perfect* (*habría sido*) -- exactly the tool a counterfactual history argument needs. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know *dejar de* + infinitive from B1 Unit 12. It says that something stopped happening or stopped being true. Here you use it for booms that ended: *El guano dejó de ser el gran negocio del Perú.*"
+    },
+    {
+      "type": "table",
+      "title": "Dejar de + infinitive",
+      "rows": [
+        [
+          "dejó de ser",
+          "stopped being"
+        ],
+        [
+          "dejó de pagar",
+          "stopped paying"
+        ],
+        [
+          "dejaron de comprar",
+          "stopped buying"
+        ]
+      ]
     },
     {
       "type": "examples",
+      "title": "In context",
       "items": [
         {
-          "spanish": "Si esos ingresos se hubieran invertido de manera sistemática en infraestructura, la historia económica del país habría sido muy distinta.",
-          "english": "If that revenue had been invested systematically in infrastructure, the country's economic history would have been very different."
-        },
-        {
-          "spanish": "Si el Perú hubiera diversificado su economía durante estas décadas, habría estado mucho mejor preparado para lo que vino después.",
-          "english": "If Peru had diversified its economy during these decades, it would have been much better prepared for what came next."
+          "spanish": "En los años 1870, el guano dejó de ser el gran negocio del Perú.",
+          "english": "In the 1870s, guano stopped being Peru's big business."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Si esos sustitutos hubieran tardado unas décadas más en desarrollarse, es posible que Perú hubiera tenido más tiempo para adaptarse.",
-          "english": "If those substitutes had taken a few more decades to develop, Peru might have had more time to adapt."
+          "spanish": "En 1876 el Estado peruano dejó de pagar la deuda.",
+          "english": "In 1876 the Peruvian state stopped paying its debt."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Si cualquiera de estos países hubiera dependido de dos o tres exportaciones, probablemente habría amortiguado mejor cada una de estas crisis.",
-          "english": "If any of these countries had depended on two or three exports, it would probably have cushioned each of these crises better."
+          "spanish": "El salitre de Chile dejó de ser tan importante.",
+          "english": "Chilean saltpetre stopped being so important."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "Both halves look back at an unreal past: *si + hubiera + participle* for the condition, *habría + participle* for the result -- never *si + habría*, which is a common learner error."
+      "content": "Always keep *de*: *dejó de ser*, never *dejó ser*. After *dejar de* comes an infinitive (*ser*, *pagar*), not a noun. *Dejar* + noun means something else: *dejó el negocio* (he left the business)."
     }
   ]
 }
diff --git a/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-revolucion-01-no-es-lo-mismo-gr.json b/content/es-latam/grammar/b1/b1-revolucion-01-no-es-lo-mismo-gr.json
index 3e4b5506..73f23966 100644
